Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: check conversation membership before storing chat
 uploads

The upload route saved the file to storage first and only afterwards checked
that the sender belonged to the conversation, so any signed-in user could fill
the bucket. It also trusted the file type reported by the browser.

- verify conversation membership before anything is stored
- detect the real image type from the file's first bytes (JPEG/PNG/GIF/WebP)
  and use it for the stored name and content type
- force messageType to IMAGE, since only images are accepted
- remove the stored file if saving the message fails
- use the shared Prisma client instead of creating one per request
